In article <2h3oas$mhe@athos.cc.bellcore.com>, nana@opal.bellcore.com (Ana Maria
Swanson) says:
>
>    I've run into kitchen sinks every so often, and wonder what can
>    be done with them.  I've dropped potions in them, kicked them, etc.
>    Am I just wasting time by trying to do anything with "#"'s?

Have you ever tried drinking from the tap?  You sometimes get a wide
variety of tap water (and occasionally some weird-tasting sewage).
It also has some similar side effects that you get from fountains.

Also, you invariably have heard tales of people accidentally dropping
rings down the sink.  In Nethack, it usually isn't accidental, and
in most cases, once it falls down the drain you can't reach to get
it back.

Well, kicking sinks Sometimes will do something interesting, among the worst
of which is summoning black puddings (awful monsters, but good eating).
Other side effects are nicer, (like kicking a ring Up the drain).

That pretty much covers most of what you can do with a sink (without
detailing all the things a sink can do to you.  One side effect that
I'll let you discover (or someone else spoil) is how a sink can be
used to get rid of certain cursed items.  Hint: it's a very deep drain.

